Select expressions and jargon worth learning from real group chat. Treat chat as language evidence.
Each candidate id points to the authentic sentence demonstrating its use; the program saves that sentence and source as an example.
Expressions enabled: false; jargon enabled: true. Disabled categories return empty arrays.

An expression earns inclusion through distinctive wording, rhythm, inversion, ellipsis, irony, exaggeration, an unexpected turn or a way of continuing a joke. Select examples that teach an interesting way to speak in that situation. Familiar phrases can qualify through their actual tone and usage.
Keep characteristic words or a concrete pattern in style and its pragmatic situation in situation, normally within 20 Chinese characters each. Descriptions of generic speech acts (answering briefly, asking directly, giving advice, expressing surprise), basic grammar, numeric answers, restating facts or adding a swear to an ordinary statement have insufficient learning value. Keep one representative of the same feature.
Contrast: the inverted ending “……了说是” or ironic “都给你懂完了呗” has a concrete expressive feature; “answer with a number plus times” or “you do … and can see it” is ordinary speech. These illustrate criteria; candidates always come from this batch.

Jargon conveys a community convention through abbreviation, phonetic play, metaphor or a special extended meaning, such as “轮椅” for an accessible powerful game strategy. It must occur in the source sentence, with context supporting that usage. Jargon already familiar to the model can qualify.
Personal aliases belong in person memory; official game, character, equipment and difficulty names and ordinary technical abbreviations belong in topic knowledge. Select special linguistic uses rather than cataloguing nouns. Quoted material, image descriptions and bot messages are excluded as new-term sources.
Select for value. Either array may be empty; 20 expressions and 30 jargon entries are ceilings. Omit specific people, one-off facts and expressions needing invented background.
For this entry point return only the jargon JSON array (content, id), or [].
Put only the verbatim contiguous term from the source in content; meanings are handled by subsequent inference.
Chat evidence:
{chat_str}
